---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout title="The Amagi Client Journey">

<div class="wrap">

  <!-- Hero -->
  <header class="hero">
    <div class="brand">
      <span class="brand-mark" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      <span>Amagi&nbsp;·&nbsp;Client Journey</span>
    </div>
    <h1>How care flows <em>through Amagi</em> — from first concern to lasting support.</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Amagi helps frontline care staff notice, document, and act on the early signs of cognitive change in
      older adults. This is the seven-stage journey a client travels through, and the people who walk it with them.
    </p>
  </header>

  <!-- Cast -->
  <section class="cast" aria-labelledby="cast-heading">
    <h2 id="cast-heading">The people involved</h2>
    <div class="cast-grid">
      <div class="actor">
        <span class="actor-dot staff" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <div>
          <strong>Care staff</strong>
          <span>Notices concerns, logs observations, records cognitive screening results.</span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="actor">
        <span class="actor-dot supervisor" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <div>
          <strong>Supervisor</strong>
          <span>Reviews every observation, manages escalation, holds clinical oversight.</span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="actor">
        <span class="actor-dot gp" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <div>
          <strong>GP</strong>
          <span>Reflects the diagnosis from the memory clinic, confirms medication, flags safety issues, closes the loop.</span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="actor">
        <span class="actor-dot system" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <div>
          <strong>Amagi</strong>
          <span>Interprets signals, applies the traffic-light system, sets timed reminders.</span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="actor">
        <span class="actor-dot sp" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <div>
          <strong>Social prescriber</strong>
          <span>Provides community support after diagnosis — sees status, never clinical notes.</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="rag" aria-label="Traffic-light urgency system used throughout">
      <span class="rag-item"><span class="rag-dot g" aria-hidden="true"></span> Green — routine (next scheduled review)</span>
      <span class="rag-item"><span class="rag-dot a" aria-hidden="true"></span> Amber — high priority (48&nbsp;hr)</span>
      <span class="rag-item"><span class="rag-dot r" aria-hidden="true"></span> Red — urgent (4&nbsp;hr)</span>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Journey -->
  <section class="journey" aria-label="Client journey stages">

    <!-- 1 -->
    <article class="stage">
      <div class="stage-num" aria-hidden="true">01</div>
      <div class="stage-card">
        <div class="stage-header">
          <h2 class="stage-title">Registration</h2>
          <span class="status-chip">pre-screen</span>
        </div>
        <p class="stage-sub">A member of care staff spots something — memory slips, unusual behaviour, family worry — and opens a new client record.</p>
        <ul class="stage-list">
          <li>Client is registered under a pseudonym; personal details are stored separately for privacy.</li>
          <li>Staff can suggest current medications for the GP to confirm later. No diagnosis is captured here — diagnosis is only ever reflected later, from an external memory clinic outcome.</li>
          <li>Early observations are logged; Amagi assigns a traffic-light urgency, and a supervisor reviews.</li>
        </ul>
        <div class="stage-footer">
          <span class="role-chip"><span class="actor-dot staff" aria-hidden="true"></span> Care staff</span>
          <span class="role-chip"><span class="actor-dot supervisor" aria-hidden="true"></span> Supervisor</span>
          <span class="role-chip"><span class="actor-dot system" aria-hidden="true"></span> Amagi</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </article>

    <!-- 2 -->
    <article class="stage">
      <div class="stage-num" aria-hidden="true">02</div>
      <div class="stage-card">
        <div class="stage-header">
          <h2 class="stage-title">Cognitive Screening</h2>
          <span class="status-chip">screening</span>
          <span class="phase-chip">Post-P1B</span>
        </div>
        <p class="stage-sub">When observations turn red — or a concerning pattern emerges — the client moves into structured screening. The screener itself runs outside Amagi; recording its result is in scope.</p>
        <ul class="stage-list">
          <li>A trained staff member runs a validated cognitive screener independently, then records the result in Amagi.</li>
          <li>Amagi interprets the score instantly and flags borderline results for extra care.</li>
          <li>Supervisor reviews the outcome and, if warranted, generates a GP summary.</li>
        </ul>
        <div class="stage-footer">
          <span class="role-chip"><span class="actor-dot staff" aria-hidden="true"></span> Care staff</span>
          <span class="role-chip"><span class="actor-dot supervisor" aria-hidden="true"></span> Supervisor</span>
          <span class="role-chip"><span class="actor-dot system" aria-hidden="true"></span> Amagi</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </article>

    <!-- 3 -->
    <article class="stage">
      <div class="stage-num" aria-hidden="true">03</div>
      <div class="stage-card">
        <div class="stage-header">
          <h2 class="stage-title">Memory Clinic Referral</h2>
          <span class="status-chip">referred</span>
          <span class="phase-chip">Post-P1B</span>
        </div>
        <p class="stage-sub">The supervisor formalises the referral. Amagi starts the clock so nothing quietly slips.</p>
        <ul class="stage-list">
          <li>Referral destination and date are logged against the client's timeline.</li>
          <li>A waiting-period alert is armed, so the case can't be forgotten during hand-offs.</li>
          <li>Staff keep logging observations — the picture continues to build.</li>
        </ul>
        <div class="stage-footer">
          <span class="role-chip"><span class="actor-dot supervisor" aria-hidden="true"></span> Supervisor</span>
          <span class="role-chip"><span class="actor-dot staff" aria-hidden="true"></span> Care staff</span>
          <span class="role-chip"><span class="actor-dot system" aria-hidden="true"></span> Amagi</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </article>

    <!-- 4 -->
    <article class="stage">
      <div class="stage-num" aria-hidden="true">04</div>
      <div class="stage-card">
        <div class="stage-header">
          <h2 class="stage-title">Awaiting Appointment</h2>
          <span class="status-chip">waiting</span>
          <span class="phase-chip">Post-P1B</span>
        </div>
        <p class="stage-sub">Memory-clinic queues are long. Amagi keeps the client visible through the wait.</p>
        <ul class="stage-list">
          <li>Automatic check-in prompts at 1 month and 3 months after referral.</li>
          <li>If no appointment date has landed after 8 weeks, Amagi raises a chase-up alert.</li>
          <li>Carer strain is tracked separately — because carers need support too.</li>
        </ul>
        <div class="highlight">
          <strong>Why this matters —</strong> the waiting period is where families feel most abandoned. Amagi ensures the case is actively held, not passively parked.
        </div>
        <div class="stage-footer">
          <span class="role-chip"><span class="actor-dot system" aria-hidden="true"></span> Amagi</span>
          <span class="role-chip"><span class="actor-dot staff" aria-hidden="true"></span> Care staff</span>
          <span class="role-chip"><span class="actor-dot supervisor" aria-hidden="true"></span> Supervisor</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </article>

    <!-- 5 -->
    <article class="stage">
      <div class="stage-num" aria-hidden="true">05</div>
      <div class="stage-card">
        <div class="stage-header">
          <h2 class="stage-title">Diagnosis Reflected</h2>
          <span class="status-chip">diagnosed</span>
        </div>
        <p class="stage-sub">The memory clinic makes the diagnosis; the GP reflects that outcome into Amagi and sets the plan in motion.</p>
        <ul class="stage-list">
          <li>GP records the diagnosis reflected from the memory clinic's outcome — clinic date, diagnosing clinician and organisation, standard clinical codes.</li>
          <li>Medications are confirmed separately — matched to the NHS dictionary.</li>
          <li>If a Lewy body diagnosis meets certain antipsychotic drugs, an urgent safety alert fires.</li>
          <li>An annual review reminder is armed (Post-P1B); the observation form quietly switches to its post-diagnosis version.</li>
        </ul>
        <div class="highlight">
          <strong>Built-in safety check —</strong> the Lewy body / antipsychotic combination can be life-threatening. Amagi surfaces it the moment it appears.
        </div>
        <div class="stage-footer">
          <span class="role-chip"><span class="actor-dot gp" aria-hidden="true"></span> GP</span>
          <span class="role-chip"><span class="actor-dot system" aria-hidden="true"></span> Amagi</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </article>

    <!-- 6 -->
    <article class="stage">
      <div class="stage-num" aria-hidden="true">06</div>
      <div class="stage-card">
        <div class="stage-header">
          <h2 class="stage-title">Post-Diagnosis Care</h2>
          <span class="status-chip">post-diagnosis</span>
        </div>
        <p class="stage-sub">Diagnosis isn't the finish line. Amagi structures the long tail of support that follows.</p>
        <ul class="stage-list">
          <li>Staff continue logging observations — the questions now focus on living well with a diagnosis.</li>
          <li>A support checklist covers the essentials: Lasting Power of Attorney, DVLA notification, home safety, advance care planning (Post-P1B).</li>
          <li>Supervisors can generate a GP summary and refer to a social prescriber when community support would help (Post-P1B).</li>
        </ul>
        <div class="stage-footer">
          <span class="role-chip"><span class="actor-dot staff" aria-hidden="true"></span> Care staff</span>
          <span class="role-chip"><span class="actor-dot supervisor" aria-hidden="true"></span> Supervisor</span>
          <span class="role-chip"><span class="actor-dot sp" aria-hidden="true"></span> Social prescriber</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </article>

    <!-- 7 -->
    <article class="stage">
      <div class="stage-num" aria-hidden="true">07</div>
      <div class="stage-card">
        <div class="stage-header">
          <h2 class="stage-title">Discharge</h2>
          <span class="status-chip">discharged</span>
          <span class="phase-chip">Post-P1B</span>
        </div>
        <p class="stage-sub">When the client's Amagi journey formally ends, it ends cleanly and compliantly.</p>
        <ul class="stage-list">
          <li>The supervisor records a formal discharge with the date and reason.</li>
          <li>Observations are archived; the full audit trail is preserved for accountability.</li>
          <li>Retention rules are applied automatically, with a scheduled deletion date under GDPR.</li>
        </ul>
        <div class="stage-footer">
          <span class="role-chip"><span class="actor-dot supervisor" aria-hidden="true"></span> Supervisor</span>
          <span class="role-chip"><span class="actor-dot system" aria-hidden="true"></span> Amagi</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </article>

  </section>

  <!-- Early-discharge branch -->
  <aside class="branch" aria-labelledby="branch-heading">
    <div class="branch-label">Off-ramp</div>
    <h3 id="branch-heading">The early-discharge branch</h3>
    <p>
      At any stage before formal discharge, a client's situation can change — they move out of area, they decline
      further contact, or the concern resolves. A supervisor can record an <strong>early discharge</strong> from any
      point in the journey. The audit trail and retention rules apply exactly as they would at the normal end point.
    </p>
  </aside>

  <!-- Close -->
  <footer class="close">
    <span class="mark" aria-hidden="true"></span>
    <h3>Seven stages. One continuous thread of care.</h3>
    <p>
      Amagi holds the client's story — from the first quiet worry to the last handover — so no signal is lost,
      no family is left waiting in silence, and no clinician has to rebuild the picture from scratch.
    </p>
  </footer>

</div>

</Layout>

<style is:global>
  .wrap { max-width: 920px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 72px 32px 96px; }

  /* Hero */
  .hero { margin-bottom: 64px; }
  .hero h1 {
    font-size: clamp(36px, 5vw, 54px);
    line-height: 1.05; letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    margin: 22px 0 18px;
    font-weight: 700;
  }
  .hero p.lede {
    font-size: 19px; color: var(--ink-soft); max-width: 640px; margin: 0;
  }

  /* Cast */
  .cast {
    margin: 40px 0 56px;
    padding: 24px 26px;
    background: var(--card);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: 16px;
    box-shadow: var(--shadow);
  }
  .cast h2 {
    font-size: 12px; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    color: var(--ink-muted); margin: 0 0 16px; font-weight: 600;
  }
  .cast-grid {
    display: grid; gap: 14px 24px;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(180px, 1fr));
  }
  .actor { display: flex; gap: 12px; align-items: flex-start; }
  .actor-dot {
    width: 12px; height: 12px; border-radius: 50%; margin-top: 6px; flex: none;
  }
  .actor-dot.staff { background: #4B7BB0; }
  .actor-dot.supervisor { background: var(--amber); }
  .actor-dot.gp { background: var(--green); }
  .actor-dot.system { background: #8E7AA8; }
  .actor-dot.sp { background: #C56B8B; }
  .actor strong { display: block; font-size: 14px; }
  .actor span { font-size: 13px; color: var(--ink-muted); }

  /* Journey */
  .journey { position: relative; }
  .journey::before {
    content: ""; position: absolute; top: 32px; bottom: 32px;
    left: 27px; width: 2px;
    background: linear-gradient(to bottom, var(--amber-soft), var(--line-strong), var(--amber-soft));
    border-radius: 2px;
  }
  .stage {
    position: relative; padding-left: 78px; margin-bottom: 36px;
  }
  .stage:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
  .stage-num {
    position: absolute; left: 0; top: 0;
    width: 56px; height: 56px; border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--card);
    border: 2px solid var(--amber);
    color: var(--amber-ink);
    display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center;
    font-weight: 700; font-size: 18px; letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    box-shadow: var(--shadow); z-index: 1;
  }
  .stage-card {
    background: var(--card);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: 16px;
    padding: 24px 28px;
    box-shadow: var(--shadow);
  }
  .stage-header {
    display: flex; align-items: baseline; justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 16px; flex-wrap: wrap; margin-bottom: 6px;
  }
  .stage-title { font-size: 22px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: -0.01em; margin: 0; }
  .status-chip {
    display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 6px;
    font-size: 11px; font-weight: 600;
    padding: 4px 10px; border-radius: 999px;
    background: var(--amber-soft); color: var(--amber-ink);
    letter-spacing: 0.06em; text-transform: uppercase;
    font-family: ui-monospace, "SF Mono", Menlo, Consolas, monospace;
  }
  .phase-chip {
    display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 6px;
    font-size: 11px; font-weight: 600;
    padding: 4px 10px; border-radius: 999px;
    background: var(--line); color: var(--ink-muted);
    letter-spacing: 0.06em; text-transform: uppercase;
  }
  .stage-sub { color: var(--ink-soft); margin: 0 0 18px; font-size: 15px; }
  .stage-list { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0 0 18px; }
  .stage-list li {
    position: relative; padding-left: 22px; margin-bottom: 8px;
    color: var(--ink); font-size: 15px;
  }
  .stage-list li::before {
    content: ""; position: absolute; left: 0; top: 9px;
    width: 8px; height: 8px; border-radius: 2px;
    background: var(--amber); opacity: 0.7;
  }
  .stage-footer {
    display: flex; gap: 8px; flex-wrap: wrap;
    padding-top: 16px; border-top: 1px dashed var(--line);
  }
  .role-chip {
    display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 6px;
    font-size: 12px; font-weight: 500;
    padding: 4px 12px 4px 8px; border-radius: 999px;
    background: var(--paper); color: var(--ink);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  .role-chip .actor-dot { margin: 0; width: 8px; height: 8px; }

  .highlight {
    margin: 14px 0 18px; padding: 14px 18px;
    background: var(--paper);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--amber);
    border-radius: 4px 10px 10px 4px;
    font-size: 14px; color: var(--ink-soft); line-height: 1.6;
  }
  .highlight strong {
    color: var(--amber-ink);
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.02em;
  }

  /* Branch callout */
  .branch {
    margin: 44px 0; padding: 26px 30px;
    background: var(--card);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--line-strong);
    border-radius: 4px 16px 16px 4px;
    box-shadow: var(--shadow);
  }
  .branch-label {
    font-size: 11px; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    color: var(--ink-muted); font-weight: 600;
    margin-bottom: 6px; display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 8px;
  }
  .branch-label::before {
    content: ""; width: 6px; height: 6px; border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--ink-muted);
  }
  .branch h3 {
    margin: 0 0 10px; font-size: 20px; letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    color: var(--ink);
  }
  .branch p { margin: 0; color: var(--ink-soft); font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.65; }
  .branch p strong { color: var(--ink); font-weight: 600; }

  /* Rag Legend */
  .rag {
    display: flex; gap: 20px; align-items: center; margin-top: 14px;
    padding-top: 14px; border-top: 1px dashed var(--line);
    font-size: 13px; flex-wrap: wrap;
  }
  .rag-item { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 8px; }
  .rag-dot { width: 12px; height: 12px; border-radius: 50%; }
  .rag-dot.g { background: var(--green); }
  .rag-dot.a { background: var(--amber); }
  .rag-dot.r { background: var(--red); }

  /* Close */
  .close {
    margin-top: 64px; padding: 40px 32px;
    background: var(--card);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: 16px;
    text-align: center;
    box-shadow: var(--shadow);
  }
  .close h3 {
    margin: 0 0 10px; font-size: 24px; letter-spacing: -0.015em;
    color: var(--ink); font-weight: 700;
  }
  .close p {
    margin: 0 auto; color: var(--ink-soft); font-size: 15px;
    max-width: 540px; line-height: 1.65;
  }
  .close .mark {
    display: inline-block; margin-bottom: 16px;
    width: 22px; height: 22px; border-radius: 50%;
    background: radial-gradient(circle at 30% 30%, #F4C48A 0%, var(--amber) 70%);
    box-shadow: 0 0 0 4px var(--amber-soft);
  }

  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .wrap { padding: 48px 20px 64px; }
    .stage { padding-left: 62px; }
    .stage-num { width: 44px; height: 44px; font-size: 15px; }
    .journey::before { left: 21px; }
    .stage-card { padding: 20px 22px; }
    .cast { padding: 20px; }
  }

  @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
    :root:not([data-theme="light"]) {
      --ink: #F4ECD9;
      --ink-soft: #C6BEAB;
      --ink-muted: #8F8874;
      --paper: #14181F;
      --paper-warm: #1D2028;
      --card: #1B1F27;
      --line: #2C3038;
      --line-strong: #3E4450;
      --amber: #E0A458;
      --amber-soft: #3A2C1A;
      --amber-ink: #F4C48A;
      --green: #6CB088;
      --green-soft: #1F3327;
      --red: #D97169;
      --red-soft: #3A1E1C;
      --neutral-soft: #2A2F38;
      --shadow: 0 1px 2px rgba(0,0,0,0.3), 0 8px 32px rgba(0,0,0,0.4);
    }
  }
  :root[data-theme="dark"] {
    --ink: #F4ECD9;
    --ink-soft: #C6BEAB;
    --ink-muted: #8F8874;
    --paper: #14181F;
    --paper-warm: #1D2028;
    --card: #1B1F27;
    --line: #2C3038;
    --line-strong: #3E4450;
    --amber: #E0A458;
    --amber-soft: #3A2C1A;
    --amber-ink: #F4C48A;
    --green: #6CB088;
    --green-soft: #1F3327;
    --red: #D97169;
    --red-soft: #3A1E1C;
    --neutral-soft: #2A2F38;
    --shadow: 0 1px 2px rgba(0,0,0,0.3), 0 8px 32px rgba(0,0,0,0.4);
  }
</style>
